---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL } from "../legal";

const sections = [
  { id: "agreement", title: "Agreement" },
  { id: "eligibility", title: "Who can use Mates" },
  { id: "account", title: "Your account" },
  { id: "mates", title: "Working with your mates" },
  { id: "acceptable-use", title: "Acceptable use" },
  { id: "connected", title: "Connected apps and GitHub" },
  { id: "content", title: "Your content" },
  { id: "plans", title: "Plans and payment" },
  { id: "availability", title: "Early access and changes" },
  { id: "ending", title: "Ending your use" },
  { id: "disclaimers", title: "Disclaimers" },
  { id: "liability", title: "Limitation of liability" },
  { id: "law", title: "Governing law" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Contact" },
];
const mail = `mailto:${LEGAL.contact}`;
---

<Legal title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using Mates and the Mates website." sections={sections}>
  <h2 id="agreement">Agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {LEGAL.operator} (“we”, “us”), who operates {LEGAL.product}, covering
    the {LEGAL.product} app, this website and the waitlist. By using any of them you agree to these terms and to our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you don’t agree, please don’t use {LEGAL.product}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="eligibility">Who can use Mates</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 13, or the minimum age in your country if higher, and able to form a binding agreement. If you use
    {LEGAL.product} for an organisation, you confirm you’re allowed to accept these terms for it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="account">Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in secure; you’re responsible for what happens in your account. Tell us at
    <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.contact}</a> if you think someone else has accessed it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="mates">Working with your mates</h2>
  <p>
    Your mates are AI. They can be wrong, incomplete or out of date, and can misunderstand what you ask. Check their work
    before you rely on it, especially for anything important such as health, legal, financial or safety matters, where
    they are no substitute for a professional.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you ask a mate to act for you, for example to draft an email, change a calendar, use a website or change code, it
    acts on your behalf and you’re responsible for those actions. Review what they prepare before it goes out. Code always
    comes back as a pull request: reviewing and merging it is your decision.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don’t use {LEGAL.product} to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law or anyone’s rights, including privacy and intellectual property;</li>
    <li>harass, deceive, impersonate or harm others, or create spam or malware;</li>
    <li>access accounts, systems or data you’re not allowed to;</li>
    <li>disrupt, overload, probe or reverse-engineer the service, or get around its limits;</li>
    <li>resell {LEGAL.product} or use it to build a competing product.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may limit or suspend use that breaks these rules or puts others at risk.</p>

  <h2 id="connected">Connected apps and GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect another service, your use of it stays subject to that service’s own terms. You give your mates
    permission to use it as you instruct, and you can revoke that at any time. We aren’t responsible for other services or
    for changes they make. For GitHub, the Mates app only works on the repositories you choose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content">Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of what you put into {LEGAL.product} and of what your mates create for you. You give us permission
    to store and process that content only as needed to run {LEGAL.product} for you, as described in the Privacy Policy.
    You confirm you have the right to share what you give us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="plans">Plans and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Paid plans, when available, are billed in advance for each monthly or yearly period, usually through the App Store or
    Google Play under their payment terms, and renew until you cancel. Cancelling stops the next renewal; you keep access
    until the end of the period you paid for. Usage limits for each plan are shown in the app. We’ll give you notice before
    any price change applies to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">Early access and changes</h2>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.product} is new and some features are early or experimental. Joining the waitlist doesn’t guarantee access or a
    launch date. We may add, change or remove features, and we’ll give notice of changes that significantly affect you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ending">Ending your use</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using {LEGAL.product} and delete your account at any time in Settings. We may suspend or end access if you
    seriously or repeatedly break these terms, or if we have to for legal reasons, and we’ll tell you unless the law or
    safety prevents it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.product} is provided “as is” and “as available”. To the extent the law allows, we make no promises that it will
    be uninterrupted, error-free, or that AI output will be accurate or fit for a particular purpose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we aren’t liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for loss of data, profits or
    business, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before it, or
    US$50 if you haven’t paid anything. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law, or your
    rights as a consumer where you live.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.country}, and disputes will be handled by the courts of {LEGAL.country},
    unless the law where you live gives you the right to bring a claim there. We’d always rather sort a problem out
    directly, so please contact us first.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. We’ll change the date at the top and tell you about significant changes before they take
    effect. Using {LEGAL.product} after that means you accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.contact}</a>. {LEGAL.product} is operated by {LEGAL.operator},
    {LEGAL.country}.
  </p>
</Legal>
